"_score_insider_buying":42.9,"pf":[],"description_full":"ICF International, Inc. provides management, technology, and policy consulting and implementation services to government and commercial clients in the United States and internationally. The Company provides consulting and technology services across several key domains, such as strategy and public policy; energy and environmental sustainability; and climate resilience; digital transformation including information technology; modernization, cloud, cybersecurity, and data analytics; health and social programs including public health and education; international development and capacity building; disaster management and recovery planning; transportation, aviation, and infrastructure; and marketing and strategic communications. The company serves energy, environment, infrastructure, and disaster recovery; health and social programs; and security and other civilian and commercial markets; U.S. federal government departments and agencies, local government departments and agencies, international governments, and commercial clients. The company was formerly known as ICF Consulting Group Holdings, LLC and changed its name to ICF International, Inc. in 2006. ICF International, Inc. was founded in 1969 and is headquartered in Reston, Virginia.","ceo_bio":"Mr. John M. Wasson | Chairman of the Board & CEO | Age 64 | Compensation: $2.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 6K people. Revenue per employee of $269K ranks in the below the sector median among Industrials peers, improving at 6%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $17K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 8\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["ICF International, Inc. is a small-cap industrials business with a $1.4B market cap on $1.9B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +2% over the past three years and +5% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 8% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically.","The business throws off $120M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 6 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.55\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.9\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 4.7\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 0.7%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Goodwill represents 61% of total assets \u2014 a large impairment risk hanging over book value","sev":"red","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 8% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Industrials ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Industrials tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 44% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"ICF (ICFI) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/icf-icfi-q3-2026-earnings-164945000.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793984250.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.153,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"ICFI Q3 Earnings Beat Estimates on Margin Gains, Revenues Miss","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3025818/icfi-q3-earnings-beat-estimates-on-margin-gains-revenues-miss?cid=CS-ZC-FT-analyst_blog%7Cearnings_article-3025818","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793981820.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.202,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"ICF International, Inc. (NASDAQ:ICFI) to Issue Quarterly Dividend of $0.14","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/icf-international-inc-nasdaqicfi-to-issue-quarterly-dividend-of-0-14.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793971853.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.67,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","dividend"]},{"title":"ICF International declares $0.14 dividend (NASDAQ:ICFI)","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4668069-icf-international-declares-0_14-dividend","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793969522.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.296,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"Critical Comparison: ICF International (NASDAQ:ICFI) & CBIZ (NYSE:CBZ)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://