 market and 46% in 2008."],"val":["The stock trades 44% below its DCF fair value of $141, a meaningful margin of safety.","The fair-value models disagree (dispersion 45%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $105 to $192 (P10-P90), so treat the estimate as noisy.","On multiples it looks cheap against Industrials peers: P/E 16.5 vs 23.3 and P/FCF 11.9 vs 22.3 (sector median).","Against its own history it is cheap: the EBIT multiple sits 14% below its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are mixed: an FCF yield of 8.4% (above the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 6.5% (vs the 8% bar).","The 4 covering analysts target $107 on average, 35% above the price."],"prof":["ROIC of 8% earns above the cost of capital of 8.0%, but the 0pp spread is short of the 7pp moat bar; returns have been steady (CV 0.16).","It converts 6% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 1.55x.","ROE of 9% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (2.0x equity multiplier).","It spends 0.9% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is moderate at 1.9x net debt to EBITDA ($5.3M of cash against $401.4M of debt), above the 1.5x gate, with interest covered 4.7x.","Goodwill makes up 61% of assets, a soft asset exposed to impairment."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 1.7% over 3 years, 4.4% over 5 years and 5.2% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating.","At current returns, reinvesting 26% of profits supports about 2.1% a year of fundamental growth, too little to drive meaningful growth.","Free cash flow has compounded -5.0% a year over five years, short of the 5% durability bar.","Forward indicators: a backlog worth 82% of annual revenue and deferred revenue up 77%.","Capex runs only 0.4x depreciation (1.2% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown.","Its Rule of 40 score is 10, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders own a modest 1.9%, and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","Insider trading is two-way: 3 purchases and 4 sales over the past year, net $1.2M sold.","Shareholder yield is a modest 0.7% (0.7% in dividends).","The share count has shrunk 1.0% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake."],"people":["With about 6,972 employees, each generates about $269K of revenue, 0.7x the Industrials median, and productivity has risen 5.9% a year.","That works out to $17K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $2.1M (8x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (1/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $3K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"INVEST","conv":71,"head":"Invest: trades 44% below fair value of $141; p/E 16.5x vs sector 23.3x.","pros":["Model rating LEAN BUY (composite 46, gates 12/25)","Trades 44% below fair value of $141","P/E 16.5x vs sector 23.3x","P/FCF 11.9x vs sector 22.3x","4 analysts' mean target $107 (+35%)"],"cons":[],"flags":[],"need":[],"buy_below":120.03,"vc":{"base":141.21,"base_src":"dcf","bear":104.61,"bull":192.45,"alt_median":53.88,"n_alt":3,"gap":2.1164,"dispersion":0.4549,"level":"LOW","why":["models disagree (45% dispersion)","DCF is 212% above the other models' median ($53.88)"]},"med":{"pe":23.2692,"ev_ebitda":13.319,"pfcf":22.2778,"pb":3.0551,"roic":0.1001,"gross_margin":0.2851,"fcf_margin":0.068,"div_yield":0.0147}},"ticker":"ICFI","date":"2026-11-06"}